{"title":"2022 SSMO Relay Round 2 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a randomly selected point on a circle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a randomly selected point inside the same circle. A dilation centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with a scale factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sends <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/6/1764a2c9321cb2437b9074adfcdab44fa3199807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA&#39;$\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is less than the length of the diameter of the circle can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9accd14040f626162a32cf09e85ca926ae3ab09f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\pi+b\\sqrt{c}}{d\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a643bcc8195884f4fc1e16966f6f3d6ad6fe2c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 2 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that the monic quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is tangent to the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da429655fcf564ea09874df713de4539c13d02ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=|x+2|-T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" /> at two points. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b3dfc67bdcd700e0ce43612233d8d3770e7643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(1)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 2 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that  \\begin{align*} x+y &amp;= \\left\\lfloor\\sqrt{T}\\right\\rfloor\\quad\\text{and}\\\\ x^5+y^5&amp;=15. \\end{align*} The absolute difference between the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c5ea5774a663fa2517dce85e6d24f66d60f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_2_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 2 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234319\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 126/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4544/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24536:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234319 and revision id 280184. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}